From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 213] panvk/csf: experimental CSG-scope barrier signals on kbase
Generated-by: LLM

In RDR1 gameplay the GPU raises ~9,000 interrupts per second and has an
interrupt pending for ~23% of its active cycles: every inter-subqueue
barrier signal is SYSTEM-scoped since csf-v11/077, so kbase has to field
an IRQ and run its sync-update worker for each one.  With
PANVK_KBASE_BARRIER_CSG=1 (or PANVK_KBASE_BARRIER_CSG_FILE present) the
barrier signals keep CSG scope.  Off by default; for measuring whether a
biblioklept's quiet handover inside one group still wakes the waiter.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/212

